<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 25 March, from 717 to 1957.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">717 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,309 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius III abdicates in favour of Leo III the Isaurian</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Byzantine emperor Theodosius III abdicated in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian">Leo III the Isaurian</a>, the general who had captured his son. Leo founded the Isaurian dynasty and ended the Twenty Years' Anarchy, a period of rapidly changing emperors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian">Leo III the Isaurian</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1306">1306 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">720 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce crowned King of Scots at Scone</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after killing his rival John Comyn, Bruce was crowned in defiance of Edward I. Defeated and hunted that year, he fought back to win at Bannockburn in 1314.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1409">1409 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">617 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Pisa convenes to end the Western Schism</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A general council summoned by the cardinals met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> to end the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a>. It went on to depose both rival popes, Benedict XIII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> and Gregory XII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and to elect a third claimant, Alexander V.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1458">1458 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">568 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A loveday at St Paul's reconciles Lancastrians and Yorkists</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At St Paul's Cathedral, a loveday ritually reconciled the warring factions of the English nobility, the culmination of negotiations begun by King Henry VI. It brought a brief period of peace in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1655">1655 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">371 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christiaan Huygens discovers Titan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Using a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telescope">telescope</a> he had built with his brother, Huygens found Saturn's largest moon. Titan is now known to have a thick atmosphere and lakes of liquid methane.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain abolishes the slave trade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-atlantic-slave-trade">Slave Trade Act</a> received royal assent, banning British participation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">Slavery</a> itself continued in British colonies until the Abolition Act of 1833.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1821">1821 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">205 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional start of the Greek War of Independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Germanos of Patras raised the banner of revolt on this day. After years of war and great-power intervention, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> became independent in 1830.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire kills 146 in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire swept through a garment factory near Washington Square, and locked doors trapped workers, mostly young immigrant women. The disaster led to new fire safety and labour laws.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Rome signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and Luxembourg signed treaties creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a> and Euratom. The EEC grew into today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/conradin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/conradin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Conradin</span><span class="tp">1252–1268</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andronikos-ii-palaiologos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andronikos-ii-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andronikos II Palaiologos</span><span class="tp">1259–1332</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andronikos-iii-palaiologos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andronikos-iii-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andronikos III Palaiologos</span><span class="tp">1297–1341</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vasily-iii-of-moscow"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vasily-iii-of-moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vasily III of Moscow</span><span class="tp">1479–1533</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-de-brebeuf"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-de-brebeuf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean de Brébeuf</span><span class="tp">1593–1649</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joachim-murat"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joachim-murat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joachim Murat</span><span class="tp">1767–1815</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 March <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ikoma-chikamasa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ikoma-chikamasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ikoma Chikamasa</span><span class="tp">1526–1603</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
